{"name":"Moosewood","hex":"#5d5744","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"moosewood","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Striped maple (Acer pensylvanicum)","Hobblebush, Viburnum lantanoides."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moosewood"}],"entries":[{"title":"Acer pensylvanicum","blocks":[{"text":"Acer pensylvanicum, known as the striped maple, moosewood, whistlewood, moose maple or goosefoot maple, is a North American species of maple. It is a small, slow-growing understory tree that can change its sex throughout its lifetime."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Moosewood_leaves.jpg/330px-Moosewood_leaves.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acer_pensylvanicum","wikidata":"Q1190312"},{"title":"Viburnum lantanoides","blocks":[{"text":"Viburnum lantanoides is a perennial shrub of the family Viburnaceae, growing 2–4 meters (6.6–13.1 ft) high with pendulous branches that take root where they touch the ground. These rooted branches form obstacles which easily trip walkers – hence the common name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/ON_-_Algonquin_Provincial_Park_-_Bl%C3%BCte.jpg/330px-ON_-_Algonquin_Provincial_Park_-_Bl%C3%BCte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viburnum_lantanoides","wikidata":"Q3114111"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Viburnum_lantanoides_nb.jpg/250px-Viburnum_lantanoides_nb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Viburnum_lantanoides_nb.jpg/500px-Viburnum_lantanoides_nb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Viburnum_lantanoides_nb.jpg/250px-Viburnum_lant